You are an on-call network engineer for a campus network that uses Google Cloud for its core routing and IPAM. You are SSH’d into a Google Cloud VM acting as the campus’s central DHCP relay and IPAM controller. A new building (Building 7) was just added to the 10.40.0.0/16 campus block, and the IPAM controller was reconfigured to serve a new /24 subnet for it. The change was pushed 30 minutes ago, but Building 7 clients are not getting DHCP leases.

You have the following configuration excerpt from the VM’s DHCP relay config (normalized for clarity):

```
subnet 10.40.7.0/24 {
    range 10.40.7.10 10.40.7.200;
    option routers 10.40.7.1;
    option domain-name-servers 8.8.8.8, 8.8.4.4;
