The VM’s primary network interface has IP 10.40.0.10/16. The campus router (on-prem, not in GCP) is configured to route 10.40.0.0/16 to the VM’s interface. The VM’s firewall (GCP VPC firewall rules) allows UDP 67/68 from the campus subnet.

A colleague suggests the issue is that the DHCP relay is not listening on the correct interface because the subnet 10.40.7.0/24 is not directly connected to the VM. They propose adding a secondary IP address 10.40.7.1/24 to the VM’s interface to fix the relay.

